decision_conditions:
Prior to the commencement of development, including demolition, site clearance, excavation or the bringing of plant or materials onto the site, a scheme of arboricultural site supervision and monitoring shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The scheme shall include: 
 
• confirmation of the appointment of a retained arboricultural consultant to undertake an auditable system of site supervision and monitoring; 
• contact details and responsibilities of the arboricultural consultant, site manager and other relevant site personnel; 
• site induction arrangements relating to tree protection; 
• a timetable of monitoring visits linked to implementation and retention of the approved tree protection measures, excavation and foundation works within the RPAs of T4 and T5, and final removal of protective measures; 
• procedures for addressing variations or unauthorised incursions into construction exclusion zones; and 
• arrangements for written and photographic monitoring records to be submitted to the Local Planning Authority within 48 hours of each site visit. 
 
The development shall thereafter be carried out in full accordance with the approved scheme. 
 
REASON: To ensure that the TPO-protected and retained trees are not damaged or otherwise adversely affected by building operations, excavation or soil compaction, and that the approved tree protection measures remain in place throughout the relevant works
